course: dictionary
lesson: 408
title: Words for things at home
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: An appliance is a machine or device that does a job in the home. You can often work out what a word means from the words around it. «You should always dry your hands before touching plugs, switches or electrical appliances.» Plugs and switches use electricity, and electrical appliances are in the same list, so they must be electric machines.
explain: «A switch can fail, so an appliance is unplugged before anyone touches the inside.» The clue is unplugged. You can only unplug something that has a plug, so an appliance is something that plugs in. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a machine that does a job is unplugged before anyone touches the inside" still makes sense.
explain: Phrases give clues too. A kitchen appliance is an appliance you use in the kitchen, and an electrical appliance is one that runs on electricity. Once you spot the pattern, you can work out new phrases like these.
fact: An appliance is a machine or device used at home to do a job.
fact: Fridges, washing machines, toasters and kettles are all appliances.
fact: An electrical appliance is an appliance that runs on electricity.
fact: Appliances change electrical energy into other kinds, such as heat in a toaster or movement in a fan.
fact: Stay safe with appliances: do not touch them with wet hands, never put metal in a toaster, and unplug an appliance before you touch its inside.
exercise: «You should always dry your hands before touching plugs, switches or electrical appliances.» What is an appliance? | *A machine or device used at home to do a job | A type of food eaten at breakfast | A kind of plant that grows in the kitchen | A loud sound made by a door
exercise: Which of these is an appliance? | A glass jar | A wooden spoon | *A kettle | A bread knife
exercise: Why should you dry your hands before touching electrical appliances? | It keeps your hands warm | Appliances need water to run | Wet hands make appliances work faster | *Water and electricity are a dangerous mix
test: What does «electrical appliance» mean? | A small toy for the bath | A machine made of wood | *An appliance that runs on electricity | A tool for cutting paper
test: Which is a safe thing to do with an appliance? | Put a knife into the toaster to get the bread out | Use it with wet hands | Touch the inside while it is still plugged in | *Unplug it before touching the inside
exam: In a science lesson, what does a toaster change electrical energy into? | Sound only | Water | Movement only | *Heat
